# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Firebase Auth configuration (all values are read from the runtime env and
# inlined into both the server and the browser bundle by Next.js).
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored) for local development, and set the same
# variables in the hosting provider (Vercel → Project → Environment Variables).
#
# Every NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_* value below is optional at build time: when a
# variable is missing the app falls back to the documented fallback project and
# says so in the console + in the in-app diagnostics panel. In production, set
# them all (an incomplete set is the most common cause of
# `auth/invalid-api-key`, `auth/configuration-not-found` and redirect failures).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# "firebase" → real Firebase Auth · "demo" → on-device gateway · "auto" → Firebase
# when the config below is complete, demo otherwise. Default when unset: demo.
NEXT_PUBLIC_AUTH_BACKEND=firebase

NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyAbb9aCsOfMkw9G5H0L58LSkbsONhix51k
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=agriculture-intelligente-7873e.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=agriculture-intelligente-7873e
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=agriculture-intelligente-7873e.firebasestorage.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=213483282746
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:213483282746:web:badde539687095497a7003
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-VKD4SWJLNJ

# Firebase Console → Authentication → Settings → Authorized domains must list
# every origin the app is served from, including the Arena preview host
# (*.e2b.app) and http://localhost:3000 for local development.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AI assistant — field-trained 2-step chain behind /api/assistant (server-only
# secrets; NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix so they are never inlined into the browser
# bundle). 100 % free: Hugging Face serverless Inference (free CPU tier) +
# the Gemini free tier.
#
# GEMINI_API_KEY       → Google AI Studio → Get API key (aistudio.google.com/apikey)
#                        Step 2 — the SOLE conversational orchestrator and
#                        final response generator: gemini-3.5-flash (→
#                        3.5-flash-lite → 2.5-flash when an id is retired) via
#                        https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/<model>:generateContent
#                        under ONE shared 18 s AbortController deadline for the
#                        whole model chain (a full Arabic answer needs 10–15 s on
#                        a cold Flash model; 9 s aborted healthy generations).
#                        It receives the system instruction, the user query,
#                        the profile context (wilaya/region, crop, role), the
#                        recent conversation history and — when a leaf photo
#                        was sent — the Step 1 ViT diagnosis (disease label,
#                        confidence score, differential / candidate diseases).
#                        A successful answer returns HTTP 200 { source: "llm" }
#                        (source: "hybrid" when it ships with a diagnosis).
#
# HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY  → Hugging Face → Settings → Access Tokens. A standard
#                        user access token works (fine-grained tokens need
#                        "Make calls to Inference Providers" ticked — a plain
#                        read token 401/403s on the router).
#                        Powers the vision side of the pipeline on the FREE
#                        serverless Inference tier:
#                        Step 0 — open object detector for leaf detection &
#                        smart cropping (DETR chain),
#                        Step 1 — the FIELD-TRAINED VISION TRANSFORMER
#                        classifier chain (the old MobileNetV2 is gone), tried
#                        in order:
#                          1. kimcomehome/plantvillage-vit-leaf-disease
#                             (ViT-base-patch16-224, ImageNet-21k pretrained,
#                             fine-tuned on PlantVillage — 38 crop-disease
#                             classes, ~99.8 % held-out accuracy);
#                          2. nateraw/vit-base-beans (ViT-base fine-tuned on
#                             the field "beans" leaf-disease dataset);
#                          3. wambugu71/crop_leaf_diseases_vit (ViT-tiny
#                             multi-crop last resort).
#                        The returned { label, score } array is parsed into
#                        the primary disease + confidence + differential
#                        diagnoses (top-3 candidates). If BOTH the ViT chain
#                        and Gemini are down, a built-in formatter still
#                        answers from the Step 1 diagnosis (source: "direct",
#                        never a 500) — that is also the only case the UI
#                        shows its amber fallback warning.
#                        HF_TOKEN and HGF_TOKEN (the conventional Hugging Face
#                        variable names) are honoured as aliases when
#                        HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY is unset/blank. With no usable
#                        token, Steps 0–1 are skipped instantly (no request,
#                        no error, no delay).
#
# Set at least one of the two keys on the server at runtime (including on
# Vercel): each step is optional and degrades to the next one. Only when BOTH
# keys are missing/blank does the route answer HTTP 503 with code MISSING_KEYS.
# Every other outcome answers HTTP 200: upstream AI failures degrade to
# built-in direct replies ({ source: "direct" }) — the API never returns 500.
# Never expose these secrets with a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS (OPTIONAL, server-only) — Step 0 "Detection &
#                        Cropping" detector chain, tried in order. Step 0
#                        runs an open-source object detector BEFORE the
#                        ViT classifier: the leaf is localised, the
#                        photo is cropped with sharp and ONLY the cropped
#                        pixels are forwarded to Step 1 (background noise —
#                        hands, soil, pots — never reaches the classifier).
#                        Default chain (open weights, free hf-inference tier):
#                        suryanshgoel/detr-finetuned-plantdoc (DETR-ResNet-50
#                        fine-tuned on the PlantDoc plant-disease dataset,
#                        every class is a plant/leaf) → facebook/detr-resnet-50
#                        (COCO fallback, plant-labelled boxes only). Override
#                        with a comma-separated list of Hub ids, e.g.:
#                        HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS=suryanshgoel/detr-finetuned-plantdoc
#                        When the detector is unavailable or finds no leaf,
#                        the untouched original frame is classified instead
#                        (the outcome is reported in the `preprocessing`
#                        field of the API response).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEMINI_API_KEY=
HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=
HF_LEAF_DETECT_MODELS=
